"[0709.3144] Inclusion Matrices and Chains (https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.3144)\nciteturn2view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.3144\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 20 Sep 2007]\nL9: # Title:Inclusion Matrices and Chains\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†E. Ghorbani , cite6†G.B. Khosrovshahi , cite7†Ch. Maysoori , cite8†M. Mohammad-Noori L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Inclusion Matrices and Chains, by E. Ghorbani and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite9†View PDF cite10†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract: Given integers $t$, $k$, and $v$ such that $0\\leq t\\leq k\\leq v$, let $W_{tk}(v)$ be the inclusion matrix of $t$-subsets vs. $k$-subsets of a $v$-set. We modify slightly the concept of standard tableau to study the notion of rank of a finite set of positive integers which was introduced by Frankl. Utilizing this, a decomposition of the poset $2^{[v]}$ into symmetric skipless chains is given.\nL17: Based on this decomposition, we construct an inclusion matrix, denoted by $W_{\\bar{t}k}(v)$, which is row-equivalent to $W_{tk}(v)$. Its Smith normal form is determined. As applications, Wilson's diagonal form of $W_{tk}(v)$ is obtained as well as a new proof of the well known theorem on the necessary and sufficient conditions for existence of integral solutions of the system $W_{tk}\\bf{x}=\\bf{b}$ due to Wilson.\nL18: Finally we present anotherinclusion matrix with similar properties to those of $W_{\\bar{t}k}(v)$ which is in some way equivalent to $W_{tk}(v)$.\nL19: Comments:  | Accepted for publication in Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series A\nL20: Subjec