ct:We prove super-polynomial lower bounds for low-depth arithmetic circuits using the shifted partials measure [Gupta-Kamath-Kayal-Saptharishi, CCC 2013], [Kayal, ECCC 2012] and the affine projections of partials measure [Garg-Kayal-Saha, FOCS 2020], [Kayal-Nair-Saha, STACS 2016]. The recent breakthrough work of Limaye, Srinivasan and Tavenas [FOCS 2021] proved these lower bounds by proving lower bounds for low-depth set-multilinear circuits.\nL17: An interesting aspect of our proof is that it does not require conversion of a circuit to a set-multilinear circuit, nor does it involve a random restriction. We are able to upper bound the measures for homogeneous formulas directly, without going via set-multilinearity. Our lower bounds hold for the iterated matrix multiplication as well as the Nisan-Wigderson design polynomials.\nL18: We also define a subclass of homogeneous formulas which we call unique parse tree (UPT) formulas, and prove superpolynomial lower bounds for these. This generalizes the superpolynomial lower bounds for regular formulas in [Kayal-Saha-Saptharishi, STOC 2014], [Fournier-Limaye-Malod-Srinivasan, STOC 2014].\nL19: Subjects:  | Computational Complexity (cs.CC); Symbolic Computation (cs.SC)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite12†arXiv:2211.07691 [cs.CC]\nL21:    | (or cite13†arXiv:2211.07691v1 [cs.CC] for this version)\nL22:    | cite14†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2211.07691†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Prashanth Amireddy [cite15†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 14 Nov 2022 19:08:22 UTC (97 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Low-depth arithmetic circuit lower bounds via shifted partials, by Prashanth Amireddy and 4 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite10†View PDF L35:   * cite11†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite16†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite17†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL4